{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-90671",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-11$ and $b=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(7-(-11))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{324}{12}=27.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
